<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>

  <!-- Settings: window category (mod-list entry) -->
  <!-- EN: Unique Melee Weapons -->
  <UMW_SettingsCategory>Armes de mêlée uniques</UMW_SettingsCategory>

  <!-- Settings: section headers. "Trait abilities" heads the tuning of the abilities some weapon
       traits grant (the word "trait" as in weapon trait, the same word as the Traits header). The
       quest section's header is "{0} quest" with {0} the warband faction's def label, capitalized
       and already localized, so it reads "Warband quest"; phrase it so the injected name needs no
       inflection. -->
  <!-- EN: Weapons -->
  <UMW_SettingsWeapons>Armes</UMW_SettingsWeapons>

  <!-- EN: Traits -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraits>Traits</UMW_SettingsTraits>

  <!-- EN: Generation -->
  <UMW_SettingsGeneration>Génération</UMW_SettingsGeneration>

  <!-- EN: Traders -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraders>Commerçants</UMW_SettingsTraders>

  <!-- EN: Trait abilities -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraitAbilities>Capacités des traits</UMW_SettingsTraitAbilities>

  <!-- EN: {0} quest -->
  <UMW_SettingsQuestSection>Quête : {0}</UMW_SettingsQuestSection>

  <!-- EN: Compatibility -->
  <UMW_SettingsCompat>Compatibilité</UMW_SettingsCompat>

  <!-- EN: The unique weapons that can be generated. A weapon that is turned off will no longer appear as a reward or in loot, and the others will take its place. Weapons already in your save are not affected. A group's box switches the whole group, and a half-filled box means some of its rows are off. Click and drag across rows to switch several at once. -->
  <UMW_SettingsWeaponsDesc>Les armes uniques qui peuvent être générées. Une arme désactivée n'apparaîtra plus en récompense ni dans le butin, et les autres prendront sa place. Les armes déjà présentes dans votre sauvegarde ne sont pas affectées. La case d'un groupe coche ou décoche tout le groupe. Une case partiellement cochée indique que certaines de ses lignes sont désactivées. Cliquez et faites glisser sur les lignes pour en cocher ou décocher plusieurs à la fois.</UMW_SettingsWeaponsDesc>

  <!-- EN: The traits that can appear on newly generated unique weapons. A trait that is turned off will no longer appear, and the others will take its place. Weapons that already carry it keep it. Every weapon must keep at least one trait it can start with, so the last one left for a weapon cannot be turned off. A group's box switches the whole group, and a half-filled box means some of its rows are off. Click and drag across rows to switch several at once. -->
  <UMW_SettingsTraitsDesc>Les traits qui peuvent apparaître sur les armes uniques nouvellement générées. Un trait désactivé n'apparaîtra plus, et les autres prendront sa place. Les armes qui le possèdent déjà le conservent. Chaque arme doit conserver au moins un trait qu'elle peut recevoir à sa création. Son dernier trait ne peut donc pas être désactivé. La case d'un groupe coche ou décoche tout le groupe. Une case partiellement cochée indique que certaines de ses lignes sont désactivées. Cliquez et faites glisser sur les lignes pour en cocher ou décocher plusieurs à la fois.</UMW_SettingsTraitsDesc>

  <!-- EN: Unique melee weapons in trader stock. Every trader is off by default. A trader that can stock them will also buy them, even while its row is off. Weapons turned off in the Weapons section never appear in stock. -->
  <UMW_SettingsTradersDesc>Les armes de mêlée uniques en vente chez les commerçants. Par défaut, aucun commerçant n'en propose. Un commerçant capable d'en proposer en achètera aussi, même si sa ligne est désactivée. Les armes désactivées dans la section « Armes » n'apparaissent jamais en stock.</UMW_SettingsTradersDesc>

  <!-- Settings: reusable label suffixes. Each includes a leading space, and every applicable one is
       appended (no precedence between them), so they must read cleanly back to back. -->
  <!-- EN:  (default) -->
  <UMW_DefaultSuffix> (par défaut)</UMW_DefaultSuffix>

  <!-- {0} is another piece of content the current value matches, named from its own def label. -->
  <!-- EN:  (same as {0}) -->
  <UMW_SameAsSuffix> (identique à {0})</UMW_SameAsSuffix>

  <!-- Checkbox-row suffixes, at most one per row, each with a leading space. The first is appended
       to a group header (which is the bare name of a mod or DLC) only while that mod or DLC is not
       installed or not enabled, so the greyed header reads "Royalty (3) (not active)". {0} in the second
       is a weapon's def label (lowercase): the row is a trait that cannot be turned off because it is
       the last trait that weapon could roll first, so the box is held on. -->
  <!-- EN:  (not active) -->
  <UMW_NotActiveSuffix> (inactif)</UMW_NotActiveSuffix>

  <!-- EN:  (last trait for {0}) -->
  <UMW_LastTraitSuffix> (dernier trait pour {0})</UMW_LastTraitSuffix>

  <!-- EN:  (requires restart) -->
  <UMW_RequiresRestartSuffix> (nécessite un redémarrage)</UMW_RequiresRestartSuffix>

  <!-- Settings: grouped rows. In the Weapons and Traits sections, the rows an optional mod or DLC
       adds sit under a header that is just that mod or DLC's name and its row count (coloured, no
       extra text), with a three-state box that switches the whole group. The first string is the
       count, with a leading space, appended to the name in the name's colour so the header reads
       "Royalty (3)"; {0} is how many weapons or traits this mod adds for that mod or DLC in that
       section, shown even while it is not active. The second is the header's tooltip; {0} is the name,
       injected already coloured: do not inflect it. The last sentence describes click-and-drag
       painting over the checkbox rows beneath the header. -->
  <!-- EN:  ({0}) -->
  <UMW_GroupCountSuffix> ({0})</UMW_GroupCountSuffix>
  <!-- EN: Everything from {0} in this section. -->
  <UMW_IntegrationGroupDesc>Tout ce qui vient de {0} dans cette section.</UMW_IntegrationGroupDesc>
  <!-- EN: Traits original to {0}. -->
  <UMW_OwnTraitsGroupDesc>Traits propres à {0}.</UMW_OwnTraitsGroupDesc>
  <!-- EN: Melee counterparts of the traits {0} gives its unique ranged weapons. -->
  <UMW_OdysseyTraitsGroupDesc>Les équivalents de mêlée des traits que {0} donne à ses armes à distance uniques.</UMW_OdysseyTraitsGroupDesc>

  <!-- Fallback display names, used only while the mod is not installed. Proper nouns: kept as published. -->
  <!-- EN: Vanilla Factions Expanded - Pirates -->
  <UMW_ModNameVfePirates>Vanilla Factions Expanded - Pirates</UMW_ModNameVfePirates>

  <!-- EN: Vanilla Textures Expanded -->
  <UMW_ModNameVte>Vanilla Textures Expanded</UMW_ModNameVte>

  <!-- Settings: Weapons. One checkbox per weapon. {0} is the weapon's own def label (lowercase), whose
       gender varies (hache unique / glaive unique) and which is absent from the vanilla WordInfo gender
       tables, so {0_gender} would silently default to masculine. The French therefore never agrees with
       {0}: it keeps every later reference on "l'arme" and puts no article in front of the placeholder. -->
  <!-- EN: Allow {0} to be generated. -->
  <UMW_WeaponEnabledDesc>Autoriser la génération de cette arme : {0}.</UMW_WeaponEnabledDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Traits. One checkbox per trait, labelled from the trait's own def label; {0} is that label (lowercase). -->
  <!-- EN: Allow {0} to appear on newly generated unique weapons. -->
  <UMW_TraitEnabledDesc>Autoriser le trait {0} à apparaître sur les armes uniques nouvellement générées.</UMW_TraitEnabledDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Generation -->
  <!-- {0} is the wood resource's item label (ThingDef WoodLog, "wood" in English, lowercase). -->
  <!-- EN: Exclude {0} from generated unique weapons -->
  <UMW_ExcludeWoodStuff>Exclure les matériaux en {0} des armes uniques générées</UMW_ExcludeWoodStuff>

  <!-- {0} is the vanilla longsword's item label (lowercase), named as the example reward. It is an
       injected label, so the French reaches it through the vanilla material frame "en bois" (Core's
       ThingMadeOfStuffLabel is "{1} en {0}") rather than an agreeing adjective, and puts no article
       in front of it. -->
  <!-- EN: When enabled, unique weapons will never be generated from wood, so a quest reward is never a wooden {0}. When disabled, wood is one of the materials a weapon can be made from. -->
  <UMW_ExcludeWoodStuffDesc>Si cette option est activée, les armes uniques ne seront jamais générées en bois, et les quêtes n'offriront plus de {0} en bois en récompense. Si elle est désactivée, le bois fait partie des matériaux possibles pour une arme.</UMW_ExcludeWoodStuffDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Traders. Both toggles default off. The row label is a shared template: {0} is the
       trader kind's own def label, capitalized ("Fournisseur militaire", "Chaman"), so it tracks
       vanilla's translation; each description's {0} is the same label in lowercase. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in {0} stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniques>Armes uniques dans le stock du {0}</UMW_TraderStocksUniques>

  <!-- EN: About half of {0} visits will bring one unique melee weapon of medieval or lower tech level. Ultratech traits never appear on its stock. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesWarMerchantDesc>Environ une visite de {0} sur deux apportera une arme de mêlée unique de niveau technologique médiéval ou inférieur. Les armes de son stock ne portent jamais de traits ultratechnologiques.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesWarMerchantDesc>

  <!-- EN: About half of {0} visits will bring one unique melee weapon of medieval or lower tech level. Ultratech traits can appear on its stock, since shamans trade in relics they do not fully understand. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShamanDesc>Environ une visite de {0} sur deux apportera une arme de mêlée unique de niveau technologique médiéval ou inférieur. Les armes de son stock peuvent porter des traits ultratechnologiques, car les chamans font commerce de reliques qu'ils ne comprennent pas entièrement.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShamanDesc>

  <!-- Outlander rows. "medieval" / "industrial" are Core TechLevel_Medieval / TechLevel_Industrial
       (médiéval / industriel), inflected as adjectives of "niveau technologique". The settlement row is fixed text:
       Core Settlement.label is "base de faction" and the outlander pawn word is "étrangers"
       (OutlanderCivil/Rough.pawnsPlural). The two combat-supplier rows recast "{0} caravan" as
       "caravane ({0})" / "de {0}", as {0} is a whole noun phrase. -->
  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in Outlander settlement stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlement>Armes uniques dans le stock des bases d'étrangers</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlement>

  <!-- EN: About one in five outlander settlements will stock one unique melee weapon of industrial or higher tech level. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlementDesc>Environ une base d'étrangers sur cinq proposera une arme de mêlée unique de niveau technologique industriel ou supérieur.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesOutlanderSettlementDesc>

  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in {0} caravan stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravan>Armes uniques dans le stock des caravanes ({0})</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravan>

  <!-- EN: About one in five {0} caravan visits will bring one unique melee weapon of industrial or higher tech level. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravanDesc>Environ une caravane de {0} sur cinq apportera une arme de mêlée unique de niveau technologique industriel ou supérieur.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesCaravanDesc>

  <!-- EN: Unique weapons in {0} trade ship stock -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShip>Armes uniques dans le stock des vaisseaux commerciaux ({0})</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShip>

  <!-- EN: About one in five {0} trade ships will carry one unique melee weapon of industrial or higher tech level. -->
  <UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShipDesc>Environ un vaisseau commercial de {0} sur cinq transportera une arme de mêlée unique de niveau technologique industriel ou supérieur.</UMW_TraderStocksUniquesShipDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Trait abilities. Each ability is a subsection headed by its own icon and name (from
       its def, already localized) followed by the first string, which names in parentheses the
       weapon trait that grants it ("Earthshake (Piledriver)"); it has a leading space and {0} is
       that trait's def label, capitalized and already localized. The ability's description is the
       header's tooltip, so the slider rows beneath name only the property: in the next three, {0}
       is the slider's current value. The unit word is part of the template, so hour- and day-based
       cooldowns are separate keys. The last row tunes a different def from the ability above it
       (the rallied buff), so it keeps the subject: {0} is that hediff's def label, capitalized; {1}
       is the value.
       French keeps the last row's {0} first, as English does, and follows it with a colon: an
       injected label placed after a preposition would want an article ("la durée de l'exaltation"),
       and its gender is unknowable here. Naming the subject first sidesteps that entirely. -->
  <!-- EN:  ({0}) -->
  <UMW_TraitAbilitySuffix> ({0})</UMW_TraitAbilitySuffix>
  <!-- EN: Cooldown: {0} hours -->
  <UMW_CooldownHours>Temps de recharge : {0} heures</UMW_CooldownHours>

  <!-- EN: Cooldown: {0} days -->
  <UMW_CooldownDays>Temps de recharge : {0} jours</UMW_CooldownDays>

  <!-- EN: Radius: {0} cells -->
  <UMW_RadiusCells>Rayon : {0} cases</UMW_RadiusCells>

  <!-- EN: {0} duration: {1} hours -->
  <UMW_HediffDurationHours>{0} : durée de {1} heures</UMW_HediffDurationHours>

  <!-- {0} is the Odyssey DLC's name, injected already coloured: do not inflect it. -->
  <!-- EN: The time the wielder must wait between earthshakes. The default matches the EMP pulser from {0}. At 0 there is no cooldown. -->
  <UMW_EarthshakeCooldownDesc>Le temps que l'utilisateur doit attendre entre deux secousses telluriques. La valeur par défaut correspond à celle du pulsar IEM présent dans {0}. À 0, il n'y a aucun temps de recharge.</UMW_EarthshakeCooldownDesc>

  <!-- EN: How far the shockwave reaches. It passes under walls but not across gaps with no floor. A wider radius will catch your own colonists too. -->
  <UMW_EarthshakeRadiusDesc>Le rayon de l'onde de choc. Elle passe sous les murs, mais ne franchit pas le vide. Un rayon plus large atteindra aussi vos propres colons.</UMW_EarthshakeRadiusDesc>

  <!-- EN: The time the wielder must wait between rallying cries. The default is long enough that a cry stays a rare moment rather than something raised in every fight. -->
  <UMW_RallyingCryCooldownDesc>Le temps que l'utilisateur doit attendre entre deux cris de ralliement. La valeur par défaut est assez longue pour que le cri reste un moment rare et ne soit pas poussé à chaque combat.</UMW_RallyingCryCooldownDesc>

  <!-- EN: How far the cry carries. Everyone in range who is not hostile and can see the wielder will be rallied. Walls block it. Sleepers in range will be woken instead. -->
  <UMW_RallyingCryRadiusDesc>Le rayon du cri. Toute personne non hostile à portée qui voit l'utilisateur sera galvanisée. Les murs le bloquent. Les personnes endormies à portée sont simplement réveillées.</UMW_RallyingCryRadiusDesc>

  <!-- EN: How long the rallied effect lasts. While it lasts, pain is halved and staggering blows are shaken off twice as fast. -->
  <UMW_RalliedDurationDesc>La durée pendant laquelle une personne reste galvanisée. Tant qu'il dure, la douleur est réduite de moitié et l'on se remet deux fois plus vite des coups qui font tituber.</UMW_RalliedDurationDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Warband quest. The section is headed by the camp's world-map icon and the
       UMW_SettingsQuestSection header above. The first string is that header's tooltip,
       describing the quest; {0} is the Odyssey DLC's name, injected already coloured: do not
       inflect it. "Ancient mercenaries" is the vanilla quest's name; translate it to match the
       official localization. The second is the slider row's label; {0} is the slider's current
       value. The desc's quest examples (ancient mercenaries, bandit camps, item stashes) are
       vanilla content names too. Taken here from the official localization. -->
  <!-- EN: A quest to raid a tribal warband holed up in an abandoned settlement. Their chief carries a unique melee weapon. Capture or kill the chief to take it. It is the low-tech counterpart of the ancient mercenaries quest from {0}. -->
  <UMW_WarbandQuestDesc>Une quête qui consiste à attaquer une bande de guerre tribale retranchée dans une colonie abandonnée. Son chef porte une arme de mêlée unique. Capturez ou tuez le chef pour la récupérer. C'est l'équivalent primitif de la quête des mercenaires anciens présente dans {0}.</UMW_WarbandQuestDesc>

  <!-- EN: Frequency: {0} -->
  <UMW_QuestCommonality>Fréquence : {0}</UMW_QuestCommonality>

  <!-- EN: How often the warband quest is offered compared with similar quests such as ancient mercenaries, bandit camps and item stashes. Higher values offer it more often. At 0 it is never offered. -->
  <UMW_WarbandQuestWeightDesc>La fréquence à laquelle la quête de la bande de guerre est proposée par rapport aux quêtes similaires, comme les mercenaires anciens, les camps de bandits et les planques. Plus la valeur est élevée, plus elle sera souvent proposée. À 0, elle n'est jamais proposée.</UMW_WarbandQuestWeightDesc>

  <!-- Settings: Compatibility. Shown only when Vanilla Textures Expanded is active. The toggle
       defaults on and is read when the game loads, hence the restart sentence. {0} is our unique
       spear's def label (lowercase); {1} is that mod's display name from its About.xml, injected so
       neither is restated here. Deliberately says nothing about performance. -->
  <!-- EN: Match the {0} to {1} -->
  <UMW_MatchVteSpear>Faire correspondre la {0} à {1}</UMW_MatchVteSpear>

  <!-- EN: {1} draws the vanilla spear longer and at a diagonal. When enabled, the {0} is turned and enlarged to match it in a drafted pawn's hands. When disabled, it keeps its own size and angle. The change is purely cosmetic and takes effect after a restart. -->
  <UMW_MatchVteSpearDesc>{1} redessine la lance de base, plus longue et inclinée en diagonale. Si cette option est activée, la {0} sera tournée et agrandie pour s'y accorder dans les mains d'un colon mobilisé. Si elle est désactivée, elle gardera sa taille et son angle d'origine. Ce changement est purement cosmétique et prend effet après un redémarrage.</UMW_MatchVteSpearDesc>

</LanguageData>
